# MCP servers (vocab / graph / pastoral)

- One server per layer. A tool belongs to exactly one server. Scaffold new tools with `new-mcp-tool`.
- Every tool declares: name, description, input JSON schema, output JSON schema, required role,
  read/write classification, and whether it touches L3 data.
- Tool inputs are validated before execution; outputs are validated and sanitised before return.
- Write tools are idempotent (accept an idempotency key) and audit-logged.
- Pastoral server: every read is scoped to `(caller_role, caller_id)`. A pastor can only read their
  own check-ins; admins can read all. Enforce in the tool, not only in the API.
- Tool descriptions are prompts — keep them precise, short, and free of instructions to the model
  beyond what the tool does.
- Tools never return secrets, internal ids of other users, or raw stack traces.
